  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Kings Corners. Logic: Shedding game with descending sequences and alternating colors.',
    Player: 'Kings Corners is a social, Solitaire-like card game played by 2 to 4 players. Build sequences of alternating colors onto a central cross-shaped layout. First to empty hand wins.',
    objective: 'Be the first player to play all cards from your hand onto the table piles.',
    gameplay: "1. Players take turns. Each turn begins with drawing 1 card from the stock.\n2. You can play any card from your hand onto a pile if it is one rank lower and a different color (e.g., a Red 7 onto a Black 8).\n3. You can move an entire pile onto another pile if the bottom card of the first fits on the top card of the second.\n4. **Kings**: If you have a King, it *must* be played into one of the empty 'Corner' slots (diagonals of the cross). Once there, it forms a new foundation pile.\n5. Empty Slots: If one of the original 4 foundation slots becomes empty, you can place any card (or sequence) there.",
    keyRules: [
      'Build sequences in descending order',
      'Alternate colors when building',
      'Kings must go to corner slots',
      'Can move entire piles onto other piles',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
