    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two to four players. The game is said to be good for four players. A standard 52-card pack is used; the first dealer is chosen at random and the turn to deal passes clockwise after each hand.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces are low (sequencing on Kings is King-Queen-Jack...2). No, wait. Standard Kings Corners Ranking: K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2-A.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Aces are low (sequencing on Kings is King-Queen-Jack...2). No, wait. Standard Kings Corners Ranking: K-Q-J-10-9-8-7-6-5-4-3-2-A.',
      dealing: "Each player is dealt 7 cards. Four cards are placed face-up in a cross (the 'T' or '+' shape). The rest form the draw pile.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Players take turns. Each turn begins with drawing 1 card from the stock.\n2. You can play any card from your hand onto a pile if it is one rank lower and a different color (e.g., a Red 7 onto a Black 8).\n3. You can move an entire pile onto another pile if the bottom card of the first fits on the top card of the second.\n4. **Kings**: If you have a King, it *must* be played into one of the empty 'Corner' slots (diagonals of the cross). Once there, it forms a new foundation pile.\n5. Empty Slots: If one of the original 4 foundation slots becomes empty, you can place any card (or sequence) there.",
